INT. THE UNSHELVED ARCHIVE - NIGHT

A hall without a floor. Books drift through the dark like slow fish, spines shimmering, pages fluttering as if in a current. Ladders lean on nothing.

YSOLDE VANTH (50s, archivist, robes of ink-stained wool, a candle in a jar on a pole) walks a path of stepping stones through the air. Behind her trails KIT HOLLOWAY (16, apprentice, bare feet, nervous), carrying an armful of loose pages.

                    YSOLDE
          Keep your eyes on the stone, not the drop.

                    KIT
          There is no drop.

                    YSOLDE
          Then you have nothing to fear.

Kit steps. The stone sinks a hair under his weight and holds. He doesn't breathe.

A book glides past, the size of a door. Its cover opens a crack, like an eye.

                    THE INDEX (V.O.)
                (resonant, everywhere)
          Query logged. Subject: Kit Holloway. Status: unregistered.

Kit stops dead. Ysolde doesn't.

                    YSOLDE
          Ignore it.

                    KIT
          It said my name.

                    YSOLDE
          It says everyone's name. Keep walking.

                    THE INDEX (V.O.)
                (resonant)
          Reason for presence?

Ysolde turns, one slow pivot of the heel. She raises the candle until it lights her chin.

                    YSOLDE
          Apprentice. Provisional. Filed under mine.

                    THE INDEX (V.O.)
                (resonant)
          Provisional entries must be stamped by the thirteenth bell.

                    YSOLDE
          I know the rule.

                    THE INDEX (V.O.)
                (resonant)
          It is the twelfth bell.

Kit swallows. Ysolde's grip on the pole tightens, white at the knuckles, but her voice remains flat as a table.

                    YSOLDE
          Then we shall be prompt.

She continues. Kit follows, steps quicker now, pages clutched to his chest. A feather of paper breaks loose; he doesn't chase it.

At the end of the path stands a lectern shaped like a tree stump. A stamp rests on it, brass, heavy. A tiny bell begins to toll, softly, from nowhere.

                    YSOLDE (CONT'D)
          Hand.

Kit presents his palm. She lifts the stamp. Holds it above his skin.

                    KIT
          Will it hurt?

                    YSOLDE
          Only afterwards.

The bell tolls again. The books around them slow, tilt, turn their covers toward the lectern like a crowd.

                    THE INDEX (V.O.)
                (resonant)
          The thirteenth bell approaches.

Ysolde brings the stamp down.
